flowchart TB
    accTitle: Settlement confirmation concurrency outcomes
    accDescr: An authorized confirmation conditionally confirms a pending settlement, creates effects once, and reloads zero-row outcomes to distinguish same-intent idempotency, competing state, and missing resources.

    Confirmation["Authorized payment confirmation"] --> Transition["Conditionally confirm pending settlement"]
    Transition --> Updated{"Row updated?"}

    Updated -->|"Yes"| Repayment["Create repayment"]
    Repayment --> Event["Publish settlement event"]
    Event --> Commit["Commit payment, settlement, outbox, and audit"]

    Updated -->|"No"| Reload["Reload trusted settlement"]
    Reload --> Outcome{"Observed outcome"}
    Outcome -->|"Same intent"| Idempotent["Idempotent success"]
    Idempotent --> NoDuplicate["Commit without duplicate effects"]
    Outcome -->|"Competing or terminal"| Conflict["SETTLEMENT_<br/>STATE_CONFLICT · 409"]
    Outcome -->|"Missing"| NotFound["SETTLEMENT_<br/>NOT_FOUND · 404"]

    Conflict --> Rollback["Roll back payment attempt and intent"]
    NotFound --> Rollback
    Rollback --> NoEffects["No repayment, outbox, notification, or audit effect"]

    Commit ~~~ Reload

    classDef error fill:#FEF2F2,stroke:#DC2626,color:#7F1D1D,stroke-width:2px
    classDef success fill:#ECFDF5,stroke:#059669,color:#064E3B,stroke-width:2px
    class Conflict,NotFound,Rollback,NoEffects error
    class Commit,Idempotent,NoDuplicate success
